  buoyancy on the 1 kg sphere at rho_off(10 cm,15 TeV): 1.3e-04 N (vertical; torque only through arm asymmetry)

(3) LINER: open Al cylinder radius R_l = 2.8/mu (28 cm at 1/mu=10 cm), height 1 m, 1 mm wall -> mass and Newtonian residual
  liner mass 4.8 kg; radial Newtonian force on a 1 kg body at x = 0, 6, 10, 15 cm off-axis (mid-height): 1.2e-25, 5.0e-11, 8.3e-11, 1.2e-10 N
  dumbbell torque cancels by symmetry; a 1 mm centring error at x=6 cm gives ~8.3e-13 N differential (F(x) slope x 1 mm)

(4) FOIL/CAN: 25 um Cu (kappa/mu >= 10 at 10 cm, 15 TeV -> full switch) disk of radius 20 cm: mass and pull on the 1 kg body at 7 cm
  foil mass 28 g; Newtonian force at 7 cm (disk, on-axis): ~6.3e-11 N  -> must be static (not switched) at Tier 1
  symmetron pull of a pinned disk on the test body (solver, disk W=0.5..1.5 at D/2): static = +1.2..1.5 v^2 > signal 1.2 v^2  -> a one-sided movable foil is NOT a usable switch
  electrostatic: unshielded two-sphere force 4.3e-12 N (dV/1 V)^2 -> a switched shield needs dV < 0.84 V for 10% of Tier 1, < 84 mV for 10% of Tier 2

(5) TIER-1 PENDULUM options: (A) 2 x 1.01 kg solid Cu spheres, 150 um W fibre; (B) 2 x 0.2 kg hollow Cu shells (3 cm, 2 mm wall), 75 um W fibre; r_arm = 6 cm, fibre 1 m
  A solid: kappa_f=7.95e-06 N m/rad, period 190 s, fibre stress 1.12 GPa (W UTS ~3 GPa), Q=3e+03: torque noise 3.6e-14 N m/rtHz -> 6.0e-13 N/rtHz, 1-h average 1.0e-14 N
      Tier-1 torque 1.8e-12 N m -> twist 0.23 urad (autocollimator 1e-8 rad: margin 23x); Newtonian F_N=2.8e-08 N -> Tier 1 is 1.1e-03 of F_N
  B hollow: kappa_f=4.97e-07 N m/rad, period 338 s, fibre stress 0.89 GPa (W UTS ~3 GPa), Q=3e+03: torque noise 1.2e-14 N m/rtHz -> 2.0e-13 N/rtHz, 1-h average 3.3e-15 N
      Tier-1 torque 1.8e-12 N m -> twist 3.62 urad (autocollimator 1e-8 rad: margin 362x); Newtonian F_N=5.5e-09 N -> Tier 1 is 5.4e-03 of F_N
  Tier-1 stability: the Newtonian torque is constant across the switch; needs 1e-3 (solid) / 5e-3 (hollow) stability per switch cycle (~1 h):
      source position 70 um / 350 um; fibre zero drift << twist (alternating on/off cancels linear drift); tilt via tiltmeter; T stability ~10 mK (calibration), ~1 mK gradient (photophoresis).
